  "content": {
    "title": "NBA Play-In Tournament bracket: 76ers secure No. 7 seed; Warriors win",
    "text": "April 14, 2026Updated April 16, 2026, 1:15 a.m. ETThe NBA postseason officially tipped off Tuesday, April 14 with two the 2026 NBA Play-In Tournament games. Two more Play-In games will take place Wednesday, April 15.In the opener, the Philadelphia 76ers secured the No. 7 playoff seed in the Eastern Conference with a 109-97 win over the Orlando Magic, who now must play the Charlotte Hornets on Friday, April 17 to decide which team earns the No. 8 seed in the East.Later, the Golden State Warriors defeated the Los Angeles Clippers in a dramatic, win-or-go-home showdown. The Warriors will face the Phoenix Suns on Friday, April 17 to determine the No. 8 playoff seed in the Western Conference.Here is the updated bracket and schedule for the 2026 NBA Play-In Tournament, along with the matchups for the first round of the NBA playoffs: Stream 2026 NBA Play-In Tournament on Prime VideoNBA Play-In Tournament results, scheduleThe losers of the No. 9 vs. No. 10 matchups will be eliminated from the postseason. The winners of the No. 7 vs. No. 8 games will solidify the No. 7 seeds in the NBA playoffs. The losers of those games will play the winners of the No. 9 vs. No. 10 matchups to claim the No. 8 seeds in the playoffs. All play-in games will be streamed exclusively on Amazon Prime Video.All times EasternTuesday, April 14East: No. 9 Charlotte Hornets 127, No. 10 Miami Heat 126 (OT)West: No. 8 Portland Trail Blazers 114, No. 7 Phoenix Suns 110Wednesday, April 15East: No. 7 Philadelphia 76ers 109, No. 8 Orlando Magic 97West: No. 10 Golden State Warriors 126, No. 9 L.A. Clippers 121Friday, April 17East: Charlotte Hornets at Orlando Magic, 7:30 p.m.West: Golden State Warriors at Phoenix Suns, 10 p.m.NBA Playoffs bracket — first-round matchupsEastern Conference(1) Detroit Pistons vs. (8) Play-In Winner(4) Cleveland Cavaliers vs. (5) Toronto Raptors(3) New York Knicks vs. (6) Atlanta Hawks(2) Boston Celtics vs. (7) Philadelphia 76ersWestern Conference(1) Oklahoma City Thunder vs. (8) Play-In Winner(4) Los Angeles Lakers vs. (5) Houston Rockets(3) Denver Nuggets vs. (6) Minnesota Timberwolves(2) San Antonio Spurs vs. (7) Portland Trail BlazersNBA Playoffs Game 1 schedules(All times Eastern)Saturday, April 18Raptors at Cavaliers, 1 p.m. | PrimeTimberwolves at Nuggets, 3:30 p.m. | PrimeHawks at Knicks, 6 p.m. | PrimeRockets at Lakers, 8:30 p.m. | ABCSunday, April 1976ers at Celtics, 1 p.m. | ABCWest No. 8 seed at Thunder, 3:30 p.m. | ABCEast No. 8 at Pistons, 6:30 p.m. | NBC and PeacockTrail Blazers at Spurs, 9 p.m. | NBC and PeacockOur editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
